      "notes": ["A shared whole-line Oracle grammar lowers exact self, attached, global, keyword-filtered, not-alone, matching-companion, other-attacker, table-wide count, per-defender count, source-controller target, named-source target, typed battlefield conditions, public monarch/poison player-state conditions, and reviewed current-turn cast, death, damage, and prior-player-attack conditions into the finite declaration solver. Current-turn facts are versioned, authoritative, hashed, reset at each turn, retained across extra combats, and preserve cast-time types and last-known logical-object/control data. Represented predicates are inviolable, defender-specific in multiplayer, projected from the same legal domains used for submission, and replay exactly. Relevant unsupported static restriction text pauses fail closed; compound, other named-target, temporary, broader, and uncompiled history predicate grammar remains blocked."]
